      "previewText": " The equilibrium constant (K) of the reaction is @@K@@: If at equilibrium, [H2] = @@concH2@@ M and [NH3] = @@concNH3@@ M, what is the concentration of N2 at equilibrium?  MAt a different temperature for this same reaction the equilibrium constant (K) is determined to be @@K2@@.At this new temperature, at equilibrium [H2] = @@conc2H2@@ and [N2] = @@concN2@@. What is the [NH3] at equilibrium for this reaction?  M",
      "targeted": [],
      "transformations": [
        {
          "children": [],
          "data": [
            {
              "children": [],
              "expression": "// Two variable definitions\nconst K = OLI.random(6.4,9.8,2) .toFixed(2);\nconst concIndex = OLI.random (0,5);\nconst conc2Index = OLI.random (0,5);\nconst arrayH = [0.200,0.250,0.300,0.350,0.400,0.450];\nconst array2H = [0.200,0.250,0.300,0.350,0.400,0.450];\nconst arrayNH3 = [0.450,0.400,0.200,0.300,0.350,0.250];\nconst concH2 = arrayH[concIndex] .toFixed(3);\nconst conc2H2 = array2H[conc2Index] .toFixed(3);\nconst concNH3 = arrayNH3[concIndex] .toFixed(3);\nconst cor1 = ((concNH3*concNH3)/(concH2*concH2*concH2));\nconst correct = (cor1/K) .toPrecision(3);\nconst corLow = correct*0.98;\nconst corHigh = correct*1.02;\nconst K2 = OLI.random(1.5,5.8,2) .toFixed(2);\nconst arrayN2 = [0.090, 0.150, 0.200, 0.250, 0.300, 0.350];\nconst concN2 = arrayN2[concIndex] .toFixed(3);\nconst cor2 = (K2*concN2*conc2H2*conc2H2*conc2H2);\nconst correct2 = (Math.sqrt(cor2)) .toPrecision(3);\nconst cor2Low = correct2*0.97;\nconst cor2High = correct2*1.03;\n\n\n// Expose variables to OLI\nmodule.exports = {\n  K,\n  concIndex,\n\n  concH2,\n  conc2H2,\n  concNH3,\n  cor1,\n  correct,\n  corLow,\n  corHigh,\n  K2 ,\n  concN2,\n  cor2,\n  correct2,\n  cor2Low,\n  cor2High\n};\n",
